From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: renaud <rlpirou@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:03:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] BTC-CORE hooks: entity census

world.entity-census.enabled, off by default, read when a world is
created. With the key off ServerLevel.btc$census is null and each of the
hunks is one null test.

- ServerLevel: the census of the world (dev.btc.core.world.EntityCensus),
  counts per category and per entity type.
- EntityCallbacks#onTrackingStart / #onTrackingEnd: the entity is counted
  in and out, on the thread of its world - spawned, loaded with its
  chunk, arrived from another world; removed, unloaded, gone.
- ServerLevel#addEntity: a spawn whose category has reached the cap set
  through BTCCoreAPI#setEntityCap is refused before its event is called,
  with the cleanup a cancelled event gets (the vehicle, the passengers
  and the entity are discarded, as CraftEventFactory#doEntityAddEventCalling
  does), for the reasons that bring a new creature into the game
  (EntityCensus.CAPPED). No reason (a journey between worlds), a plugin,
  a command, a conversion, a bucket: never refused. No cap is set by
  default, so nothing is refused unless a plugin asks.
  The vehicle is discarded only when it was made for the spawn
  (EntityCensus#madeForSpawn: not in the world yet, or added this tick).
  One that lived in the world before stays: Zombie#finalizeSpawn puts a
  baby on a chicken that is there, and a cap refuses far more often than
  an event is cancelled. That chicken is no longer marked as a jockey's
  either, which would let it despawn.
- NaturalSpawner#spawnCategoryForPosition: the cap is asked before the
  mob is made and finalized, so a natural spawn that addEntity would
  refuse draws nothing and takes nothing from the world. The rest of the
  group, one type, is given up. A baby ocelot is asked as NATURAL there:
  its own reason is only known once it is finalized.
- Animal#spawnChildFromBreeding: the cap is asked before the breed event
  and before the parents are aged, rewarded and given experience; a
  refused breeding resets their love, as a cancelled event does.
- Fox.FoxBreedGoal#breed and VillagerMakeLove#breed, the two breedings
  that do not go through Animal#spawnChildFromBreeding: the same question
  at the same place, before their breed event. A refused villager child
  gives its bed back, as a cancelled event does.

BTC addition; nothing is ported.

